From 54847c6eb75e74ff15bbbd65efbab6d36b18da8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pad: the settings panels drag anywhere and stay where left
 (0116)

Both editor bars (button settings, HUD settings) used to sit
centred at the top, covering the - / + / menu cluster, so the +
and - could not be tapped to select them. Each bar now drags by
its title or blank area (UIPanGestureRecognizer), keeps its place
in NSUserDefaults DmPadPanelPos as fractions of the view, and opens
at the left of the screen, low, clear of every control. The layout
clamps a bar inside the view, so it can never be dragged off and
lost. A slider, button or the segmented control keeps its own
touch: the pan only starts on the bar's background, title or hint.
This 0116 is the draggable settings panels, not the frame-rate
unlock the number was once reserved for (that was cancelled and
never written).
